@@ -541,6 +541,30 @@ remain allocated in this experimental integration. Matching ownership
 witnesses does not justify enabling it by default: native timing and removal
 of that redundant storage remain required.
 
+### On-demand terrain dirty queues
+
+The run-store path uses `RunnerObservedDirtyQueue` for the spatial-refresh and
+collision queues. The two independent order stamps live in the terrain's
+mutable records. A mark prepends by assigning a new stamp; removal clears it.
+Actor stamps are held separately. No linked dirty-queue record is maintained
+for a terrain cell. Size and membership are synchronous observations.
+
+The first ordered read builds a newest-first projection. Removals leave holes
+in that projection; marks invalidate it. A consuming pass advances past holes
+without sorting again. Following a callback, the successor is read from the
+current order before the current membership is removed, matching the linked
+reference. Newly prepended entries are not retroactively revisited. A failed
+refresh retains the current membership and every completed mutation prefix.
+Queue clear does not reset the monotonic order clock.
+
+Pending stamps must be cleared before typed slot reuse. Source storage is
+enumerated independently of live identity enumeration, so terminal-failure
+observations do not silently omit a pending record. Projection storage is
+bounded and preallocated; this trades linked-list maintenance for materializing
+order at the first read. Native query-bearing timing is required as well as
+selector-free generation timing: the latter cannot prove that the deferred
+work fits the first query's budget.
+
 Generated terrain may bind one initialized-birth transaction. The run store
 allocates the typed identity first, and the built-in collision owner completes
 ordinary birth publication before executing `terrainCreateProperties`. Create
